# This file is generated by dune, edit dune-project instead
opam-version: "2.0"
version: "0.1.0~alpha1"
synopsis: "Protobuf runtime for the OCaml chain libraries"
description: """
The ocaml-protoc-plugin 6.2.0 runtime, vendored with its ppx pre-expanded,
plus tools/gen-protobuf.sh -- the shared protoc invocation that generates
bindings for a consuming repository.

The package proper cannot be depended on: building its code generator needs
ppx_expect, ppx_inline_test, omd and conf-protoc, and that cone makes
`opam monorepo lock` fail outright, so a unikernel could not vendor its
dependencies at all. The runtime alone is base64 + ptime and neither depends
on unix, so this links into a MirageOS/Solo5 guest.

Generated bindings are NOT here: they belong to whichever repository owns the
schema, and are committed there so that building it needs no protoc. Only the
runtime and the generator invocation are shared. See lib/protobuf/README.md."""
maintainer: ["Gil Bahat <bahat.gil@gmail.com>"]
authors: ["Gil Bahat <bahat.gil@gmail.com>"]
license: "ISC"
homepage: "https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-web3-codec"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-web3-codec/issues"
depends: [
  "dune" {>= "3.0"}
  "ocaml" {>= "4.14"}
  "base64" {>= "3.1.0"}
  "ptime"
  "odoc" {with-doc}
]
build: [
  ["dune" "subst"] {dev}
  [
    "dune"
    "build"
    "-p"
    name
    "-j"
    jobs
    "@install"
    "@runtest" {with-test}
    "@doc" {with-doc}
  ]
]
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-web3-codec.git"
